# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DBiz Intelligence Plane — ignore rules
#
# Directory-type entries are anchored with a trailing "/" so they cannot shadow
# a source or governance FILE of the same name (e.g. build.ts, coverage.json).
# Source, documentation, ADRs, governance evidence and lockfiles are never
# ignored — see the explicit guards at the foot of this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Dependencies ---
node_modules/

# --- Build output ---
dist/
build/
out/
generated/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Caches ---
.cache/
.vite/
.turbo/
.next/
.eslintcache

# --- Scratch / temporary ---
temp/
tmp/

# --- Logs ---
logs/
*.log

# --- Test, coverage and report output ---
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
allure-results/
allure-report/
artifacts/
screenshots/

# --- OS metadata ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Editor / IDE ---
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Secrets and per-instance runtime state ---
# Env/secret files must never be committed to the Intelligence Plane (INV-6, E-5 non-retention).
# Configuration is read from the process environment (see run-server.mjs / the deployment secret store).
.env
.env.*
# The environment TEMPLATE is bootstrap configuration, not a secret: every value is a placeholder or a
# labelled local-only throwaway (ADR-0060 closes "no .env.example" as a defect). It must survive the
# .env.* glob above, or a clean clone cannot run `docker compose up`. Keep this negation after the glob.
!.env.example
# Per-instance signing secret + registration OTC store (hashes + audit). Dev-instance state only;
# production uses a secret manager / shared store (ADR-0036). Never committed.
.session-secret
# Per-instance ed25519 package-signing key (ADR-0035 Software Update Management). Dev-instance only;
# production loads/persists the key on the state mount / a secret manager. Never committed.
.package-signing-key.pem
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
/registration/
# Per-instance tenant SSOT (tenants/<slug>/tenant.json) — dev/runtime state written by the launcher.
# Same class of file-backed runtime state as /registration/ and generated/. Production persists it on
# the state mount (Azure Files /state), never in the repo. Never committed.
/tenants/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never-ignore guards. These re-include paths that a broad rule above must not
# capture. Keep them last; git applies the last matching pattern.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!package-lock.json
!package.json
!docs/**
!docs/adr/**
!governance/**
!program/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated supply-chain evidence — build output, never source (ADR-0063).
# The SBOM is derived from the resolved dependency graph and regenerated on
# every gate run and every CI build; the repository stores only the generator
# (governance/supply-chain/generate-sbom.js), not its output. Its committed copy
# was removed. This rule MUST sit after the !governance/** guard above: git
# applies the last matching pattern, so it has to follow the re-include to win.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
governance/supply-chain/sbom.cdx.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated governance EVIDENCE — regenerated on every run-all / CI run, never
# source (ADR-0063). Each verify-*.js REGENERATES its evidence and refuses a
# stale one (R-14.2, "produced by this run, not left behind"); verify-traceability
# regenerates the two matrices via generate-matrices.js. Committing these produced
# only churn (47 were dirty at audit time) and the risk of gating on a historical
# claim. The repository keeps the generators; the evidence is produced, not stored.
#
# These rules MUST follow the !governance/**, !program/** guards above — last
# matching pattern wins. Scoped so they never capture the consumed BASELINES that
# ARE source: governance/verification/proofs.json (fault-injection registry) and
# governance/closure/baseline.json (programme-closure baseline), nor the
# hand-authored program/MULTITENANCY_REVIEW/08_COMPLIANCE_MATRIX.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
governance/**/evidence.json
governance/**/*-evidence.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ONE EXCEPTION, AND IT IS AN EXCEPTION TO THE REASON RATHER THAN TO THE RULE.
#
# Every pattern above rests on one premise: the evidence can be regenerated, so
# storing it buys churn and the risk of gating on a historical claim. That premise
# is true of all 57 artefacts under governance/ except this one.
#
# ADR-0077 §5, in the ADR's own words: "CU-6a is measurable ONCE, on a tree where
# both paths exist, and RC-4'(3) preserves that measurement by digest rather than by
# re-running it." After §6 step 6 deletes the legacy modules there is no second
# implementation to compare against — so this file is not a cache of a computation,
# it is the ONLY RECORD THAT THE COMPUTATION EVER HAPPENED.
#
# Two consequences, and the second is the dangerous one:
#   · ignored, it does not survive a clean clone, so RC-4'(3) is red for everyone
#     but the machine that ran the measurement — and RC-4' permits the legacy
#     modules to be absent ONLY where this evidence is present and current.
#   · that red invites the repair that destroys the evidence: REGENERATING IT ON A
#     POST-DELETION TREE. With one path left there is nothing to compare, and what
#     such a run writes is a document, not a measurement. A green gate would then
#     assert an equivalence nobody ever measured.
#
# Tracked for the same reason as the two baselines named above — it is CONSUMED
# evidence, not produced output. Debt D-085.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!governance/capability/authoring-equivalence-evidence.json

governance/traceability/ARCHITECTURE-COVERAGE-MATRIX.md
governance/traceability/ENTERPRISE-TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md
packages/contracts/compat/evidence.json
program/ENGINEERING_SCORECARD.md
program/PLATFORM_MATURITY.md
